    {t:'match',d:M,A:['1. Citric acid','2. &alpha;-Ketoglutaric acid','3. Succinic acid','4. Acetyl CoA'],B:['a. 2C','b. 4C','c. 5C','d. 6C'],o:['1-d, 2-c, 3-b, 4-a','1-c, 2-d, 3-b, 4-a','1-d, 2-c, 3-a, 4-b','1-a, 2-b, 3-c, 4-d'],e:'Carbon numbers.'},
    {t:'match',d:H,A:['1. Isocitrate &rarr; &alpha;-ketoglutarate','2. Succinyl-CoA &rarr; succinate','3. Succinate &rarr; fumarate','4. Acetyl CoA + OAA &rarr; citrate'],B:['a. CoA released','b. FADH<sub>2</sub> formed','c. GTP formed','d. NADH + CO<sub>2</sub>'],o:['1-d, 2-c, 3-b, 4-a','1-c, 2-d, 3-b, 4-a','1-d, 2-c, 3-a, 4-b','1-a, 2-b, 3-c, 4-d'],e:'Step products.'},
    {t:'match',d:M,A:['1. NADH per turn','2. FADH<sub>2</sub> per turn','3. CO<sub>2</sub> per turn','4. Carbons in citric acid'],B:['a. 6','b. 2','c. 1','d. 3'],o:['1-d, 2-c, 3-b, 4-a','1-c, 2-d, 3-b, 4-a','1-d, 2-c, 3-a, 4-b','1-a, 2-b, 3-c, 4-d'],e:'3 NADH, 1 FADH<sub>2</sub>, 2 CO<sub>2</sub> per turn; citric acid is 6C.'},
    {t:'cistate',d:M,qtype:'CORRECT',s:['1. The TCA cycle occurs in the cytoplasm.','2. Citrate is isomerised to isocitrate.','3. Acetyl CoA combines with citric acid.','4. The TCA cycle forms 3 FADH<sub>2</sub> per turn.'],o:['Statement 2','Statement 1','Statement 3','Statement 4'],e:'Only 2 is correct.'},
    {t:'cistate',d:M,qtype:'INCORRECT',s:['1. The link reaction releases CO<sub>2</sub>.','2. GTP is converted to GDP with synthesis of ATP.','3. Mg<sup>2+</sup> is needed by pyruvate dehydrogenase.','4. NADH is formed at four points in the TCA cycle.'],o:['Statement 4','Statement 1','Statement 2','Statement 3'],e:'Three points in the cycle.'},
    {t:'s12',d:M,s1:'Statement I: The complete oxidation of pyruvate leaves three molecules of CO<sub>2</sub>.',s2:'Statement II: This process takes place in the mitochondrial matrix.',ans:'CC',e:'Both NCERT.'},
    {t:'s12',d:H,s1:'Statement I: Passing of electrons to O<sub>2</sub> takes place in the matrix.',s2:'Statement II: The TCA cycle needs regeneration of NAD<sup>+</sup> and FAD<sup>+</sup>.',ans:'IC',e:'Electron passage is on the inner membrane.'},
    {t:'combo',d:M,q:'Which are formed in one turn of the Krebs&rsquo; cycle? (a) 3 NADH (b) 1 FADH<sub>2</sub> (c) 1 GTP (d) 1 O<sub>2</sub>',o:['(a), (b) and (c) only','(d) only','(a) and (d) only','All four'],e:'No O<sub>2</sub> is formed.'},
    {t:'combo',d:H,q:'Which are required for continued operation of the TCA cycle? (a) Replenishment of OAA (b) Regeneration of NAD<sup>+</sup> (c) Regeneration of FAD<sup>+</sup> (d) Light',o:['(a), (b) and (c) only','(d) only','(a) and (d) only','All four'],e:'Light is not needed.'},
    {t:'seq',d:M,q:'Arrange the Krebs&rsquo; cycle intermediates in order:',steps:['A. &alpha;-Ketoglutaric acid','B. Citric acid','C. Succinic acid','D. Malic acid'],o:['B-A-C-D','A-B-C-D','B-C-A-D','B-A-D-C'],e:'Citrate &rarr; &alpha;-KG &rarr; succinate &rarr; malate.'}
